-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the local representation realised in the adelic span
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$ and a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform, i.e. $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the two Hecke recursions at prime powers according as the prime divides $M$ or not) and no proper divisor $M'\mid M$, $M'\neq M$, carries a normalised eigenform whose coefficients at primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Fix a prime $q$ and a function $\Phi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb{Q}$ which is an adelic lift of $g$: $\Phi$ is left invariant under the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and at every adelic matrix $h$ with trivial finite part and archimedean component in $\mathrm{GL}_2^{+}(\mathbb{R})$ one has $\Phi(h)=(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$. Assume that for all characters $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb{Q}_q^\times\to\mathbb{C}^\times$, every $\mathbb{C}$-linear map from [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ to the principal series carrier [`LocalNewvector.PSCarrier`](def/LocalNewvector_PrincipalSeriesCarrier.html#L173) $q\,\mu_1\,\mu_2$ commuting with the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-action is zero. Let $V$ be a complex vector space with a distributive $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-action commuting with scalars, such that the subspace of vectors fixed by the congruence subgroup [`FLT.SmoothVectors.gl2CongruenceSubgroup`](def/RepTheory_GL2CongruenceSubgroup.html#L181) $q\,1$ (matrices $g$ with all entries of $g-1$ and of $g^{-1}-1$ of $q$-adic norm at most $q^{-1}$) is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$, and let $f:V\to$ [`LocalNewvector.AdelicSpan`](def/LocalNewvector_AdelicSpanCarrier.html#L82) $\Phi$ be an injective $\mathbb{C}$-linear $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-equivariant map whose range is the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$-orbit of the distinguished element of the adelic span given by $\Phi$ itself. Then $V$ is irreducible in the sense of [`LocalNewvector.IsIrreducibleGLRep`](def/LocalNewvector_ConductorDatum.html#L102): $V$ contains a nonzero vector, and every $\mathbb{C}$-submodule of $V$ stable under $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_q)$ is either $\bot$ or $\top$.
--
--   This is the irreducibility statement for the local component at $q$ of the automorphic representation generated by an adelic lift of a weight-two newform, in the case where the vanishing of all equivariant maps to principal series carriers rules out principal series and special components. It feeds the analysis of the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-reduction representation, being used in [`CuspForm.IsNewform.gl2ReductionRep_toSubmodule_eq_top_of_ne_bot_of_forall_linearMap_psCarrier_eq_zero`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.gl2ReductionRep_toSubmodule_eq_top_of_ne_bot_of_forall_linearMap_psCarrier_eq_zero).
